<title>SWEDEN: Assa Abloy Q1 profit rises 44 pct.</title>
<headline>Assa Abloy Q1 profit rises 44 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997,</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			    100.5 vs    69.7</p>
<p> Sales				     1,368.3 vs 1,124.2</p>
<p> Shr (crowns)				 1.08 vs    0.81</p>
<p> Costs of goods sold		     872.6 vs   714.8</p>
<p> Administration costs		    349.2 vs   301.6</p>
<p> Goodwill writedown			 17.4 vs    10.7</p>
<p> Operating profit			  129.1 vs    97.1</p>
<p> Net financial items	    CHARGE  30.6 vs    28.0  CHARGE</p>
<p> Interest in associates		    2.0 vs     0.6</p>
<p> Tax					    29.9 vs    21.1</p>
<p> Net profit				   70.6 vs    48.6</p>
<p>NOTE -- Sweden's Assa Abloy AB produces locks and security equipment.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
